# =============================================================================
# Shop / self-hosted Docker — static build (`npm run build`)
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.production.local` (gitignored) on the machine that builds `dist/`.
#
# 1) Point the SPA at your self-hosted Kong URL + anon key from the Docker stack root `.env`:
#
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste-ANON_KEY-from-docker-root-.env
#
# For tablets on the LAN, use the shop PC IP instead, e.g. http://192.168.1.10:8000
# and set the same base URL in Docker `.env` → SUPABASE_PUBLIC_URL, API_EXTERNAL_URL, SITE_URL.
#
# 2) Admin → Data sync (hosted Supabase) is merged at build time from `.env.cloud.local`
#    (same file as `npm run dev:cloud`). Put hosted URL + anon there, OR set explicitly:
#
# VITE_SYNC_CLOUD_URL=https://your-ref.supabase.co
# VITE_SYNC_CLOUD_ANON_KEY=your-hosted-anon-key
#
# 3) On a second PC, after copying this file to .env.production.local + .env + .env.cloud.local:
#    npm run second-pc:setup
#    npx serve -s dist -l 8080
#
